! An H2 molecule along z in a 12-bohr box under a saw-tooth field (tefield)
! along z, eamp = 0.01 Hartree a.u. (about 5 V/A). The saw-tooth falls back
! over crystal z in [0.9, 1.1], 4 bohr from the nearer atom, so the molecule
! sits in its rising part and feels a uniform field. One k-point at Gamma on
! the whole sphere (automatic 1 1 1), so real-time propagation runs on it.
! The real-time check of notes/incompat/I101.md: the ground state is
! stationary under no pulse, and the response to a slow pulse is the
! static polarizability at the same frozen potential.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tefield = .true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 12.0,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'fixed'
    nbnd = 4
    edir = 3
    eamp = 0.01
    emaxpos = 0.9
    eopreg = 0.2
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.5
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (bohr)
 H 6.0 6.0 5.3
 H 6.0 6.0 6.7
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 1 0 0 0
